cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or the derived catalogs from this repository,
  please cite the methodology paper (Bibb 2026, PASP-102415) and this
  software archive.
type: software
title: >-
  sparc-shells-relaxed: Relaxed-Cap Shell Catalog with Constrained-Run
  Validation and Multi-Body Decomposition under DGC Scaling
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-05-23
authors:
  - given-names: Ron
    family-names: Bibb
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1153-2464'
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, derived catalogs, and methodology validation outputs for
  Paper III of the SPARC shells series. Extends the Paper I methodology by
  relaxing the shell-width cap (σ/r) from 0.4 to 0.8, increasing the maximum
  shell count from 2 to 5, adding hierarchical mass-to-light marginalization,
  producing a constrained-during-fit companion catalog (DGC + Hill + 1%
  M_central), and reporting implied IMBH populations under DGC scaling as
  bookkeeping (one possible interpretation, with explicit caveats). Includes
  per-galaxy strict↔relaxed classification across 102 baseline galaxies and
  the primary 123-galaxy relaxed-cap catalog with multi-body decomposition
  columns.
repository-code: 'https://github.com/RonBibb/sparc-shells-relaxed'
url: 'https://github.com/RonBibb/sparc-shells-relaxed'
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - dark matter
  - galaxy rotation curves
  - galaxy dynamics
  - SPARC
  - intermediate-mass black holes
  - Bayesian model selection
  - black hole-halo connection
  - phenomenological models
  - astrostatistics
